Firmware verification
=====================

There is one normal firmware environment:

    platformio run -e esp32-s3-hab

Connect UART0 at 115200 baud to inspect normal diagnostics. Startup reports the
watchdog, LittleFS/image queue, LoRaWAN policy, WSPR policy, and GPS wait state.
Camera captures, storage failures, WSPR frames, joins, and uplink errors also
report through the same serial connection.

Storage recovery is intentionally part of the normal boot path. For destructive
power-cut testing, interrupt external power during JPEG writes, telemetry writes,
queue/progress commits, packet transmission, and image cleanup. On reboot,
partial/unpaired files should be removed, complete file pairs should be
recovered, and the image queue should remain usable. Use a disposable device or
filesystem image for these tests.
